  sim-volume/s).
- Volume budget: accumulator += flow_rate/V_w*dt; want = floor(accumulator). Carries the fraction;
  never reset on zero flow (only on Reset/seed).
- Arclength credit: axial += exit_speed*dt; release a layer each time axial >= particle_spacing
  (decrement by spacing), placing the layer at depth = residual axial below the nozzle.
- Volume-consistent layer count: N_layer = ceil(A_eff*spacing/V_w); throughput
  (exit_speed/spacing)*N_layer >= flow/V_w so backlog stays sub-layer.
- Clamp-before-decrement: accumulator -= emitted count (not want); recipe overflow warns+clamps.
- Backlog drains in drawdown (gate: flow>0 OR accumulator>=1; uses last_exit_speed when flow=0).
- Emitted particles: phase=0, pos.w=1, chem=(0,pour_t,0,0), vel=dir*exit_speed; disc over
  r_eff=sqrt(discharge_coeff)*nozzle_radius via golden angle; written into the active pool range,
  active_count grows, phase_mirror grows, total_emitted_water_mass tracks.

